KG42.register("rules-bf953f6ffbe969ce64a6c285",{"id":"26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R008","paper":"26-battery_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"Charges for discharging the central battery and compensation for charging it enter the local-allocation objective as additional monetary components. Scope: Pool Hub local-allocation objective with centrally owned community storage. The allocation objective minimises grid-consumption costs plus central-battery discharge costs minus charging compensation. Internal P2P trade costs do not affect the community objective value. Scope: Pool Hub community allocation optimisation with centrally owned storage. Allocations obey the central battery's physical limits and a shared storage balance that aggregates charging and discharging flows across all houses. Scope: Pool Hub allocation feasibility with one shared central battery.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"settlement.payment","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Pool Hub allocation feasibility with one shared central battery. | Pool Hub community allocation optimisation with centrally owned storage. | Pool Hub local-allocation objective with centrally owned community storage.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_G","symbol":"G^{(t,h)}","meaning":"Grid consumption of house h in time step t in the Pool Hub clearing problem; a model decision variable entering the grid-cost term of Eq. (11).","kind":"operational","domain":"Grid-consumption quantity for each house h and time step t; the supplied evidence does not state an explicit numeric domain or separate nonnegativity condition.","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14"]},{"variable_id":"x_D","symbol":"D^{(t,h)}","meaning":"Discharge from the centralised battery attributed to house h in time step t; the source labels D as discharge of the battery and Eq. (12) sums D over houses for the central battery.","kind":"operational","domain":"Discharge flow for each house h and time step t; rate bounds are referred to Eqs. (7)-(9), but the exact central-battery printed rate-limit expression is not present in the supplied evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"variable_id":"x_C","symbol":"C^{(t,h)}","meaning":"Charge flow into the centralised battery attributed to house h in time step t; the source labels C as charge of the battery and Eq. (12) sums C over houses for the central battery.","kind":"operational","domain":"Charge flow for each house h and time step t; rate bounds are referred to Eqs. (7)-(9), but the exact central-battery printed rate-limit expression is not present in the supplied evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t","h"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"variable_id":"x_S","symbol":"S^{(t)}","meaning":"Overall storage level of the centralised community battery in time step t, the aggregate state variable in Eq. (12).","kind":"operational","domain":"Storage level of the centralised battery at time step t; bounded by the physical limits referenced from Eqs. (7)-(9), whose central-battery form is not printed in the supplied evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_p_G","symbol":"p_G^{(t)}","meaning":"Price of electricity from the grid in time step t; the exogenous grid-price parameter multiplying G^{(t,h)} in Eq. (11).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_p_D","symbol":"p_D^{(t)}","meaning":"Central-battery discharge price in time step t as printed in Eq. (11). Other supplied passages use a house-indexed p_D^{(t,h)} and describe the discharge price as p_{p2p}^{(t,h)} + p_C^{(t)}; the exact indexing is unresolved in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e17"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_p_C","symbol":"p_C^{(t)}","meaning":"Compensation rate for charging the central battery in time step t; Eq. (11) subtracts p_C^{(t)} C^{(t,h)} from the objective. The text states charging is compensated at the wholesale spot price, but no explicit equality is printed in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e17"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_eta_c","symbol":"\\eta^c","meaning":"Charging efficiency coefficient for the centralised battery in Eq. (12); the source states the constants differ from the private battery, but the central-battery numeric value is not given in the supplied evidence.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_eta_d","symbol":"\\eta^d","meaning":"Discharging efficiency coefficient for the centralised battery in Eq. (12), entering as 1/\\eta^d; the central-battery numeric value is not given in the supplied evidence.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_s_lower","symbol":"\\underline{s}","meaning":"Lower bound on the central battery storage level, one of the physical constants referred to via Eqs. (7)-(9) as applied to the centralised battery; the central-battery value is not printed in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_s_upper","symbol":"\\bar{s}","meaning":"Upper bound on the central battery storage level, one of the physical constants referred to via Eqs. (7)-(9) as applied to the centralised battery; the central-battery value is not printed in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_alpha","symbol":"\\alpha","meaning":"Maximum charging rate constant for the central battery, referred to via Eqs. (7)-(9) with a different value for the centralised battery; the exact central-battery value is not printed in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_beta","symbol":"\\beta","meaning":"Maximum discharging rate constant for the central battery, referred to via Eqs. (7)-(9) with a different value for the centralised battery; the exact central-battery value is not printed in the supplied excerpts.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Charges for discharging the central battery and compensation for charging it enter the local-allocation objective as additional monetary components. Scope: Pool Hub local-allocation objective with centrally owned community storage.","expression":"\\min \\sum_{h} \\left( \\sum_{t} \\left[p_G^{(t)} \\cdot G^{(t,h)}\\right] + \\sum_{t} \\left[p_D^{(t)} \\cdot D^{(t,h)}\\right] - \\sum_{t} \\left[p_C^{(t)} \\cdot C^{(t,h)}\\right] \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_G","x_D","x_C"],"parameter_refs":["theta_p_G","theta_p_D","theta_p_C"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The allocation objective minimises grid-consumption costs plus central-battery discharge costs minus charging compensation. Internal P2P trade costs do not affect the community objective value. Scope: Pool Hub community allocation optimisation with centrally owned storage.","expression":"\\min \\sum_{h} \\left( \\sum_{t} \\left[p_G^{(t)} \\cdot G^{(t,h)}\\right] + \\sum_{t} \\left[p_D^{(t)} \\cdot D^{(t,h)}\\right] - \\sum_{t} \\left[p_C^{(t)} \\cdot C^{(t,h)}\\right] \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_G","x_D","x_C"],"parameter_refs":["theta_p_G","theta_p_D","theta_p_C"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g02-e18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Allocations obey the central battery's physical limits and a shared storage balance that aggregates charging and discharging flows across all houses. Scope: Pool Hub allocation feasibility with one shared central battery.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_S","x_C","x_D"],"parameter_refs":["theta_s_lower","theta_s_upper","theta_alpha","theta_beta","theta_eta_c","theta_eta_d"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The shared central-battery storage balance updates the aggregate storage level from the previous time step using efficiency-weighted sums of all houses' charging and discharging flows.","expression":"S^{(t)} = S^{(t-1)} + \\eta^c \\cdot \\sum_{h} C^{(t,h)} - (1/\\eta^d) \\cdot \\sum_{h} D^{(t,h)}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_S","x_C","x_D"],"parameter_refs":["theta_eta_c","theta_eta_d"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Market specific constraints","anchor_text":"A. Lüth et al. Grid consumption Battery discharge Battery charge re ⎛    ⎞ min ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the Pool Hub case with a centralised storage, costs arise for three components: grid consumption, P2P trade and discharging the centralised battery. Furthermore, we compensate prosumers for charging and considers their incomes from P2P trade, see Fig. 2(b). The objective function of the Pool Hub, Eq. (11), needs hence two more components that add costs for battery discharging D^{(t,h)} and compensations for charging C^{(t,h)}. \\min \\sum_h \\left( \\sum_t [p_G^{(t)} \\cdot G^{(t,h)}] + \\sum_t [p_D^{(t)} \\cdot D^{(t,h)}] - \\sum_t [p_C^{(t)} \\cdot C^{(t,h)}] \\right) (11)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Market specific constraints","anchor_text":"A. Lüth et al. Grid consumption Battery discharge Battery charge re ⎛    ⎞ min ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The big battery is limited to the physical constraints formulated in Eqs. (7)–(9) with the constants \\underline{s}, \\bar{s}, \\alpha, \\beta, \\eta^c and \\eta^d being different for the greater centralised storage entity. The overall storage level will no longer be depending on a single house’s charge or discharge, but takes into account the sum of all flows from and to all houses to the battery. Eq. (12) comprises the sums of discharge D^{(t,h)} and charge C^{(t,h)} for the centralised battery and adds these up to the overall storage level S^{(t)}. S^{(t)} = S^{(t-1)} + \\eta^c \\cdot \\sum_h C^{(t,h)} - (1/\\eta^d) \\cdot \\sum_h D^{(t,h)}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T. (12)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Pool Hub market results","anchor_text":"ho Half of the demand can be covered from distributed generation • an within the community. sy ra 4.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The Pool Hub market design considers an interconnected community of consumers with a central storage device. P2P trade is priced at the same dynamic rate as in the Flexi User case. As the storage is no longer owned privately, discharging from the central battery will be priced and charging compensated. Charging the battery from the grid is not allowed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p09-c1r3__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.4 Comparison","anchor_text":"Fig. 4. Demand cover for exemplary houses on changed the generation and demand proﬁles of the houses","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"As trade costs do not affect the objective value of the community, the match of aggregated supply and demand influences the results."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e17","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1.4 Electricity prices","anchor_text":"step. Since this P2P price should not consider the fees for network and sp grid usage (typically one","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For the Pool Hub market, we need two more dynamic price schemes. As the charging of the central battery should be compensated, prosumers receive the wholesale spot price for electricity when they charge the battery. The discharging is priced according to each house’s willingness to pay (i.e. the P2P price p_{p2p}^{(t,h)}) plus an additional fee to avoid arbitrage operation through the battery. This additional fee is set equal to the charging compensation p_C^{(t)} at this time. Thus, the price for discharging is equal to the sum of the P2P trade price p_{p2p}^{(t,h)} and the charging compensation p_C^{(t)} and differs among the houses."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","quote":"The objective function of the Pool Hub, Eq. (11), needs hence two more components that add costs for battery discharging D^{(t,h)} and compensations for charging C^{(t,h)}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","quote":"As the storage is no longer owned privately, discharging from the central battery will be priced and charging compensated."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","quote":"\\min \\sum_h \\left( \\sum_t [p_G^{(t)} \\cdot G^{(t,h)}] + \\sum_t [p_D^{(t)} \\cdot D^{(t,h)}] - \\sum_t [p_C^{(t)} \\cdot C^{(t,h)}] \\right) (11)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","quote":"As trade costs do not affect the objective value of the community, the match of aggregated supply and demand influences the results."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","quote":"The big battery is limited to the physical constraints formulated in Eqs. (7)–(9)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","quote":"The overall storage level will no longer be depending on a single house’s charge or discharge, but takes into account the sum of all flows from and to all houses to the battery."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e2293e53ad99a673efa16f07655c78709cecdb383fffb9337771e5e000cffa20","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Provisional formalization from unreviewed B candidate evidence. Eq. (11) supports the Pool Hub clearing objective with grid-consumption cost, central-battery discharge cost, and negative charging compensation; Eq. (12) supports the aggregate central-battery storage balance. The supplied text only references the central-battery versions of Eqs. (7)-(9) rather than printing them, and Eq. (11) prints p_D^{(t)} while other passages use p_D^{(t,h)}. C003 therefore remains not_formalized for the physical-limit algebra, while the explicit balance is recorded as C004. No independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x_G","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"G is an operational grid-consumption decision of the clearing problem and enters the Eq. (11) objective under clearing.local. No settlement edge is used because G itself is not the payment relation."},{"object_id":"x_D","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"D is an operational central-battery discharge quantity in the Pool Hub clearing problem. Its priced discharge term is part of the settlement-payment-to-clearing linkage asserted by E001 and C001."},{"object_id":"x_C","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"C is an operational central-battery charging flow in the Pool Hub clearing problem. Its compensated term is part of the settlement-payment-to-clearing linkage asserted by E001 and C001."},{"object_id":"x_S","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"S is the aggregate storage state in the shared central-battery balance Eq. (12), a clearing feasibility variable; it is not itself a settlement-payment object."},{"object_id":"theta_p_G","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_G is the exogenous grid-price parameter multiplying G in the Eq. (11) objective, bound to the clearing node where the objective is formed."},{"object_id":"theta_p_D","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"p_D is the central-battery discharge price multiplying D in Eq. (11). It belongs to the monetary component linking settlement.payment to clearing.local through E001."},{"object_id":"theta_p_C","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"p_C is the charging compensation rate multiplying C with a negative sign in Eq. (11). It belongs to the monetary component linking settlement.payment to clearing.local through E001."},{"object_id":"theta_eta_c","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\eta^c is an efficiency coefficient in the aggregate storage-balance Eq. (12); it constrains clearing feasibility and is not a settlement-price object."},{"object_id":"theta_eta_d","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\eta^d is a discharging efficiency coefficient in Eq. (12), entering as 1/\\eta^d; it constrains clearing feasibility and is not a settlement-price object."},{"object_id":"theta_s_lower","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\underline{s} is a physical lower-bound constant referenced for the central battery's storage constraints in C003; it binds to clearing.local as a feasibility parameter."},{"object_id":"theta_s_upper","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\bar{s} is a physical upper-bound constant referenced for the central battery's storage constraints in C003; it binds to clearing.local as a feasibility parameter."},{"object_id":"theta_alpha","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\alpha is a physical charging-rate constant referenced for the central battery via Eqs. (7)-(9) in C003; it binds to clearing.local as a feasibility parameter."},{"object_id":"theta_beta","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\beta is a physical discharging-rate constant referenced for the central battery via Eqs. (7)-(9) in C003; it binds to clearing.local as a feasibility parameter."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"Eq. (11) is the clearing objective and includes the central-battery discharge cost and charging compensation as monetary components. E001 is the settlement-payment-to-clearing link carrying those components into clearing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R008-E001"],"rationale":"Eq. (11) is the allocation objective under clearing.local; it includes the priced battery components and omits internal P2P trade payments. E001 is the relevant settlement-to-clearing linkage for the monetary components."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Eq. (12) is a shared central-battery state-update and feasibility relation within clearing.local; no settlement-payment edge is needed for the storage balance."}],"revision_requests":["B re-extraction is required for the exact central-battery versions of Eqs. (7)-(9): the supplied text only states that the big battery is limited to the physical constraints of Eqs. (7)-(9) with different constants, and does not print the central-battery bounds and rate-limit expressions for S^{(t)}, C^{(t,h)} and D^{(t,h)}. This prevents full formalization of C003.","Resolve the discharge-price indexing inconsistency: Eq. (11) prints p_D^{(t)}, while Table 1/Table 4 and the page-7 price scheme use p_D^{(t,h)} and derive a house-specific discharge price from p_{p2p}^{(t,h)} + p_C^{(t)}. C001 and C002 transcribe Eq. (11) using p_D^{(t)} exactly as printed.","Confirm whether the absence of an explicit P2P trade term in Eq. (11) is intentional: the preceding text names P2P trade as one of three cost components, while v141-b-g03-E11 states that trade costs do not affect the community objective value.","Supply the central-battery numerical values or definitions for \\underline{s}, \\bar{s}, \\alpha, \\beta, \\eta^c and \\eta^d, and the numerical or time-series definitions of p_G^{(t)}, p_D^{(t)} and p_C^{(t)} if these are to be treated as fixed parameters rather than symbolic inputs.","B evidence remains UNREVIEWED; these revision requests identify source-level gaps and ambiguities without asserting that B transcription or downstream science has passed independent source review."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
